# BELT AND BRACES. `files: ["dist","README.md","LICENSE"]` in package.json is an
# ALLOW-LIST and already decides this; an allow-list is the control, because a
# deny-list catches only the leaks you imagined. This file exists anyway for the
# reason `voidly-worker@0.1.0` shipped a live `.env` for five months: npm
# resolves ignore rules at the PACKAGE root and never looks up a level, so the
# repo's own .gitignore is not in play here. `scripts/check-tarball.mjs` checks
# the RESULT rather than either intent.
#
# Without either, `npm pack` bundles every test file and the mainnet harness.
src/
tests/
scripts/
*.tsbuildinfo
tsconfig.json
vitest.config.ts
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.map
NOTES-internal.md
